  <body>
    <front><contents /></front>
    <chapter>
      <heading>
        Software documentation for the TTIOFastqReader class
      </heading>
      <class name="TTIOFastqReader" super="NSObject">
        <declared>TTIOFastqReader.h</declared>
        <desc>
          <p>
            <em>Inherits From:</em> NSObject
          </p>
          <p>
            <em>Conforms To:</em> NSObject (NSObject)
          </p>
          <p>
            <em>Declared In:</em> Import/TTIOFastqReader.h
          </p>
          <p>
            FASTQ importer. Parses 4-line records into unaligned
            <code>TTIOWrittenGenomicRun</code> instances.
            Internal storage is always Phred+33 ASCII.
          </p>
          <p>
            Phred encoding is auto-detected by inspecting the
            qualities byte range. Override with the
            <code>forcedPhred</code> argument.
          </p>
          <p>
            gzip-compressed input is auto-detected.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Cross-language equivalents:</strong>
            <br /> Python:
            <code>ttio.importers.fastq.FastqReader</code> <br />
            Java:
            <code>
              global.thalion.ttio.importers.FastqReader
            </code>
          </p>
        </desc>
        <method type="uint8_t" factory="yes">
          <sel>detectPhredOffsetFromBytes:</sel>
          <arg type="NSData*">qualities</arg>
          <desc>
            Phred-offset detection heuristic over a
            quality-bytes sample. @param
            <var>qualities</var> Concatenated quality bytes.
            @return <code>33</code> or <code>64</code>.
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="TTIOWrittenGenomicRun*" factory="yes">
          <sel>readFromPath:</sel>
          <arg type="NSString*">path</arg>
          <sel>forcedPhred:</sel>
          <arg type="uint8_t">forcedPhred</arg>
          <sel>sampleName:</sel>
          <arg type="NSString*">sampleName</arg>
          <sel>platform:</sel>
          <arg type="NSString*">platform</arg>
          <sel>referenceUri:</sel>
          <arg type="NSString*">referenceUri</arg>
          <sel>acquisitionMode:</sel>
          <arg type="TTIOAcquisitionMode">acquisitionMode</arg>
          <sel>outDetected:</sel>
          <arg type="uint8_t*">outDetected</arg>
          <sel>error:</sel>
          <arg type="NSError**">error</arg>
          <desc>
            Parse the FASTQ file. @param <var>path</var> FASTQ
            file <var>path</var>. @param <var>forcedPhred</var>
            <code>0</code> = auto-detect, otherwise must be
            <code>33</code> or <code>64</code>. @param
            <var>sampleName</var> Sample tag for the run. @param
            <var>platform</var> Platform tag. @param
            <var>referenceUri</var> Reference URI to record.
            @param <var>acquisitionMode</var> Run-level
            acquisition mode. @param <var>outDetected</var>
            Optional out-parameter receiving the offset
            actually applied. @param <var>error</var>
            Out-parameter populated on failure. @return
            The unaligned run on success, or <code>nil</code> on
            failure.
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="TTIOWrittenGenomicRun*" factory="yes">
          <sel>readFromPath:</sel>
          <arg type="NSString*">path</arg>
          <sel>forcedPhred:</sel>
          <arg type="uint8_t">forcedPhred</arg>
          <sel>sampleName:</sel>
          <arg type="NSString*">sampleName</arg>
          <sel>platform:</sel>
          <arg type="NSString*">platform</arg>
          <sel>referenceUri:</sel>
          <arg type="NSString*">referenceUri</arg>
          <sel>acquisitionMode:</sel>
          <arg type="TTIOAcquisitionMode">acquisitionMode</arg>
          <sel>outDetected:</sel>
          <arg type="uint8_t*">outDetected</arg>
          <sel>progress:</sel>
          <arg type="TTIOProgressBlock">progress</arg>
          <sel>error:</sel>
          <arg type="NSError**">error</arg>
          <desc>
            Progress-aware overload of {@link
            readFromPath:forcedPhred:sampleName:platform:referenceUri:acquisitionMode:outDetected:error:}. Fires {@code progress(readsDone, -1)} every {@link TTIOFastqReaderProgressIntervalReads} records during the parse phase, and a final {@code progress(total, total)} once the record count is known. Pass {@code <code>nil</code>} for {@code <var>progress</var>} to skip all callbacks; existing callers are unaffected. @param <var>progress</var> Optional <var>progress</var> block. {@code <code>nil</code>} = no callbacks.
          </desc>
        </method>
      </class>
    </chapter>
